In /backend, build the complete authentication system:

1. POST /api/auth/login
   - Accepts email + password
   - bcrypt password comparison
   - Returns accessToken (15min expiry) + refreshToken (7d expiry)
   - Stores refresh token in Redis with userId as key
   - Updates lastLoginAt on User
   - Returns user object (no password) with role, name, dealerId, zoneId

2. POST /api/auth/refresh
   - Accepts refreshToken in body
   - Validates against Redis
   - Issues new accessToken + rotates refreshToken

3. POST /api/auth/logout
   - Deletes refresh token from Redis

4. Middleware: authenticate
   - Validates Bearer JWT in Authorization header
   - Attaches req.user = { id, role, dealerId, zoneId, name }

5. Middleware: authorize(...roles)
   - Checks req.user.role is in allowed list
   - Returns 403 if not

6. Middleware: dealerScope
   - If req.user.dealerId is set, automatically appends dealerId filter to all queries
   - Dealer users cannot access data outside their dealerId

7. Rate limiting middleware using express-rate-limit:
   - Auth endpoints: 10 requests per minute
   - API endpoints: 200 requests per minute

8. Input sanitization middleware using express-validator

9. Error handling middleware — returns consistent { success: false, error: { code, message } } shape

10. Request logging middleware — logs method, path, status, duration

