Build the geo-assignment and zone management system:

ZONE MANAGEMENT (Admin only):
- GET /api/zones — list all zones with salesperson counts
- POST /api/zones — create zone with name + GeoJSON polygon coordinates
- PUT /api/zones/:id — update polygon, name
- DELETE /api/zones/:id — only if no active salespersons
- GET /api/zones/:id/salespersons — list salespersons in zone

ASSIGNMENT ENGINE (service: /backend/src/services/assignment.service.ts):

function assignSalesperson(leadLat: number, leadLng: number, dealerId?: string): Promise<User>

Logic:
1. Find which zone contains the lead coordinates using point-in-polygon algorithm (use the 'point-in-polygon' npm package with zone GeoJSON boundaries)
2. Get all active SALESPERSON users in that zone (filtered by dealerId if applicable)
3. For each salesperson, count their active leads (status NOT in [WON, LOST])
4. Pick the salesperson with the fewest active leads (load balancing)
5. If tie, calculate Haversine distance from each tied salesperson's last known location (from their most recent AttendanceLog) and pick the nearest
6. If no salesperson in zone, expand to adjacent zones (zones sharing polygon edges), repeat step 3–5
7. If still none, assign to the salesperson with fewest active leads across all zones
8. Return assigned User, log the assignment reason in TimelineEvent

GEO UTILITY FUNCTIONS (/backend/src/utils/geo.ts):
- haversineDistance(lat1, lng1, lat2, lng2): number — returns meters
- isWithinRadius(centerLat, centerLng, pointLat, pointLng, radiusMeters): boolean
- pointInPolygon(lat, lng, polygonCoords: [number,number][]): boolean
- getAddressCoordinates(address: string): Promise<{lat, lng}> — uses Google Maps Geocoding API
- reverseGeocode(lat, lng): Promise<string> — returns formatted address

