Given a RoofSection and panel dimensions, auto-place panels:

export function generatePanelLayout(input: {
  roofPolygon: Point[],          // in meters, relative to roof center
  obstructions: Point[][],
  panelWidthM: number,           // e.g. 1.134m for 580W
  panelHeightM: number,          // e.g. 2.278m
  tiltDeg: number,
  azimuthDeg: number,
  rowSpacingMultiplier?: number, // default 1.5 (1.5× panel height for shadow clearance)
  edgeSetbackM?: number,         // default 0.5m from roof edge
  orientation: 'PORTRAIT' | 'LANDSCAPE',
}): PanelLayoutResult

PanelLayoutResult = {
  panels: PanelPosition[],        // array of placed panels
  count: number,
  coveredAreaSqFt: number,
  layoutEfficiency: number,       // panels_area / usable_roof_area
}

PanelPosition = {
  id: number,
  x: number, y: number,          // center position in meters
  row: number, col: number,
  isShaded: boolean,             // from shadow analysis
  stringId: number,              // which string this panel belongs to
}

Algorithm:
1. Rotate coordinate system to align with azimuth
2. Apply edge setback (shrink polygon inward by setbackM)
3. Grid-fill with panel dimensions + row spacing
4. For each potential panel position: check if panel bounding rect is inside roof polygon (not in obstruction)
5. Assign strings: fill row by row, max panels per string from string config
6. Return all valid panel positions

Shadow clearance row spacing:
  shadowFreeDistance = panelHeight × cos(tiltDeg) + panelHeight × sin(tiltDeg) / tan(sunElevationAngle)
  sunElevationAngle for Delhi winter solstice noon ≈ 32° (28.6° latitude - 23.5° declination)

